Packaging notes for mmassx
==========================

This reintroduces mass spectrometry tooling to Debian, previously
packaged as "mmass" (removed from unstable 2019-10-18, ITP was #525675).
Upstream is now https://github.com/SCIENCE-OPEN/mmassx, an actively
maintained Python 3 fork.

Known TODOs before upload:

 * File a fresh ITP against wnpp (the old bug is closed) and reference
   it in debian/changelog.
 * Verify exact Debian package names/versions for wxPython 4.1 bindings
   (python3-wxgtk4.0 is a guess based on the current Debian archive;
   confirm against the mmassx environment.yml pins).
 * mmass.py resolves its own submodules via a path relative to the
   current working directory (`sys.path.insert(0, './mspy')`), not
   relative to the script location. debian/mmassx.wrapper works around
   this with `cd /usr/lib/mmassx` before invoking python3; if
   upstream fixes this to use `os.path.dirname(__file__)`, the wrapper
   can be simplified.
 * mspy/calculations is a mandatory C extension with no Linux build
   support upstream (only a Windows .pyd is shipped); fixed via
   debian/patches/0001-fix-linux-build-of-calculations-extension.patch
   and compiled in override_dh_auto_build. Because of this the whole
   app tree lives under /usr/lib/mmassx rather than /usr/share/mmassx,
   and the package is Architecture: any, not all.
 * gui/config.py still hardcodes version = '5.5.0' even at the v6.0.1
   tag; worth reporting upstream, and worth double-checking before
   picking the packaged version number for each new release.
 * No automated test suite upstream; dh_auto_test is a no-op.
 * Get this reviewed by the Debichem team (debichem-devel@alioth-lists.debian.net)
   before targeting an actual Debian upload; team maintenance under
   https://salsa.debian.org/debichem-team/ is the eventual home for
   this if they agree to take it on.
